# the portable toolchain: large, reproducible, never versioned
.toolchain/
# build output
**/bin/
**/obj/
# per-build archives (binaries; the source each one holds is the point, but they are large)
versions/
# runtime droppings
*.log
*.error.log

# scratch from the toolchain proof and the browser probe
.cscprobe/
probe/chromeprofile*/

# the upstream snapshot downloaded for comparison: it belongs to that project, not this one
new/
# working notes and artwork kept beside the source rather than in it - the folder at the top of this checkout,
# not every folder called icon: the rule without the leading slash also swallowed probe/icon, which is a probe
# rather than artwork and belongs in the repository.
#
# The contents are excluded rather than the folder, so that the one file in there that the program does ship can
# be named back in: a rule on the folder itself stops git from looking inside it at all, and no later rule can
# bring anything in it back.
/icon/*
# the file the program's icon is drawn from, and the one piece of that folder that belongs to this program
!/icon/曲线调整_curve-adjustment.svg
